  "title": "Monty NDE 19",
  "date": "1968",
  "content": "I was standing at the opened hood of a car on which I had just rebuilt and reinstalled a carburetor. I had my girlfriend start the car, and then there was a backfire explosion. I was covered in gasoline-soaked clothing, so I was severely burned and eventually spent four months on a burn unit. The NDE took place in about the first one or two seconds of my burn. In the first second, not only was my whole life replayed before my eyes, but also incredibly, it all started with fishy things that I was among. Then I progressed to higher levels of animal life. Next, I went through swinging freely with great grace through trees, etc. I went through the whole evolutionary spectrum leading up to man; all in a microsecond, then an overview rerun of my life up until that very moment I watched this like a movie, completely relaxed but energized too.",
